7 . This order will remain operative subject to compliance of the following conditions by the appellant :-
"i) The appellants will comply with all the terms and conditions of the bond executed by them;
ii) The appellants will cooperate in the investigation/trial, as the case NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2025:MPHC-JBP:70247 4 CRA-11410-2025 may be;
iii) The appellants will not indulge themselves in extending inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the facts of the case so as to dissuade him/her from disclosing such facts to the Court or to the Police Officer, as the case may be;
Seeta Devi vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 19 December, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/58844489/
2 iv) The appellants shall not commit an offence similar to the offence of which they are accused;
v) The appellants will not seek unnecessary adjournments during the trial;
vi) The appellants shall mark their presence before the concerned Police Station on every Saturday till conclusion of the trial;
vii) The appellants will not leave India without previous permission of the trial Court/Investigating Officer, as the case may be.
viii) If any of the aforesaid conditions is violated, then this order shall loose its effect automatically."

opennyai_summary.decision:
They are ready and willing to abide by all the terms and stringent conditions which may be imposed by this Court.
